From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ophuscado <postbox@ophuscado.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 05:34:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] vulkan: q4_0 and q8_0 matrix-vector in ggml-metal's
 layout

GGML_VK_MMV_SIMD=1 runs the q4_0 and q8_0 matrix-vector products, plain
and MUL_MAT_ID, through mul_mat_vec_simd.comp: each invocation keeps a
fixed slice of a block (half a q4_0 block, a quarter of a q8_0 block)
and its part of B in registers for every row of the workgroup, and q4_0
reads its quants by mask alone against a prescaled B, as
kernel_mul_mv_q4_0_f32 and kernel_mul_mv_q8_0_f32 do. One column only: B is reloaded per column,
so batches of 2-16 tokens keep mul_mat_vec.comp (with the shader there,
Llama 2 Q4_0 at 8-12 tokens fell from ~170 to 19-41 t/s). Unset,
nothing changes.

On an M2 Ultra under macOS, one q4_0 4096x14336 matrix-vector takes
37 us on Metal and 100 us as the Vulkan shader; f16 is near parity
(143 and 161 us), so the shader's per-weight work is the gap.
